    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d432-a1">

                <pb facs="0403" n="287" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg287"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure—Translation.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister for Foreign Affairs to Minister
                        Hartman.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ministry for Foreign Affairs</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Quito</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-11-04">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 4, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Minister for Foreign Affairs presents his compliments to his excellency the
                    Minister of the United States, and has the honor to inform him, in reply to his
                    memorandums relating to the passport requested for the native Chinese and
                    American citizen Goo Kwai, that, since this matter would involve for Ecuador a
                    precedent which might bring complications in the future, the President of the
                    Republic has not wished to decide it without first submitting it to the study
                    and consideration of the Secretary of State at Washington through the Legation
                    of Ecuador at said city.</p>
                <p>R. H. Elizalde avails himself [etc.]</p>
            </div>
        </body>
